    "hypothesis": "Deploy revision 44 (image bump python:3.12-alpine -> python:3.12.7-alpine) at ~17:51:50 UTC broke checkout container config validation. Every new task ECS launches post-deploy immediately dies with 'fatal: configuration invalid' (8+ distinct task IDs failing same way, starting 17:52:31 UTC, ~seconds after deploy registered). Old pre-deploy tasks (2831b44..., 859f784...) keep heartbeating fine, so ECS holds old tasks up while retrying failed replacements, producing tasks_running(3) != tasks_desired(2) and deployments_in_flight=2 alarm. Likely cause: new minor image (3.12.7) changed base env/config parsing behavior, or config/secret injected assumes old image layout, breaking startup validation.",
